                <pb facs="0818" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00 Presidential Campaigns/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-02T11:00:00-04:40">April 2, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:48 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. The National and Progressive Parties last night formally nominated Velázquez
                    for President and Morales for Vice President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
